+# Colour guards and exceptions
+
+**Rule:** theming flows only through tokens (`scripts/color/palette.mjs` → `tokens.generated.*` → Tailwind).
+
+| Need | Use |
+|---|---|
+| DOM / Tailwind | token classes (`bg-surface…`, `text-success`, `shadow-card`) — never `dark:` pairs for colour or elevation |
+| SVG attributes, inline `style`, DOM marker styles | `rgb(var(--success-graphic))`, `rgb(var(--overlay) / 0.6)` |
+| `<canvas>`, MapLibre paint properties | `tokenHex()` / `tokenRgba()` from `@/lib/themeColors`; re-paint with `subscribeTheme()` |
+| PDF, print, e-mail HTML, QR | resolved hex from `BRAND_COLORS` (`tokens.generated.ts`) or an allowlisted file |
+
+## Guard (`npm run lint:colors`)
+* Zero tolerance: raw Tailwind palette classes, palette-scale classes on UI utilities, `text-white/black` on solid status fills.
+* Literals (`#hex`, `rgb()`, `hsl()`) are allowed only in files listed in `scripts/color/color-allowlist.json`, each with a documented
+  category and a `max` that can only decrease. `// color-ok: <reason>` allows a single line.
+* `node scripts/color/check-colors.mjs --update-baseline` lowers `max` / drops cleaned files; it never adds files.
+
+## Tests
+* `scripts/color/contrast.test.ts` — every declared fg/bg pair in 4 themes; generated files up to date.
+* `scripts/color/guards.test.ts` — allowlist integrity, elevation tokens in every theme block.
+* `src/lib/themeColors.test.ts` — token resolver.
+* `e2e/color-contrast-routes.spec.ts` — axe `color-contrast` on 25 routes × light/dark, plus light/dark structure parity.
+* `e2e/color-visual.spec.ts` — visual snapshots (first run: `--update-snapshots`).
+
+## Known remaining exceptions
+See `docs/design/color-inventory.md` (generated). Largest: persisted categorical palettes (zones, door outcomes, graph kinds) that need a
+data migration to viz tokens; tenant brand data; documents/print; the token documentation page.
+Not covered by tokens yet: MapLibre colours in `CanvassMap` are resolved at layer creation (no live theme repaint, unlike `LiveMapCanvas`).
